// GLM-5's decoder layer up to its MLP on one TP8 rank for M = 1 .. 4, 6, 8, 12 and 16 tokens (MTP's draft extend on
// requests of 2 to 6 tokens each, a request's tokens consecutive), in the layers that run the
// DSA indexer: the residual stream through input_layernorm, qkv_a (q_a, the kv latent, k_pe), the
// q_a and kv RMSNorms and this rank's q_b; the indexer's q, k and head weights, the tokens' keys
// stored into the paged index-K cache, each token's scores over its positions and their top-2048 as
// KV slots through its page table (all of them, in position order, when there are no more);
// q_latent = q_nope W_UK, RoPE (interleaved) on q_pe and k_pe, the tokens' fp8 KV rows stored into
// the cache at their slots, each token's attention over those slots' rows, the tokens' own rows
// from this call, W_UV, then o_proj, summed over the ranks of the peer memory in rank order and
// added to the stream. GLM-5.2-MXFP4's MTP draft layer's weights: qkv_a, q_b, the indexer's,
// o_proj, W_UK and W_UV bf16 (row-major, as sglang holds them; W_UK and W_UV without a scale).
// Infera-Flash's attn_qkv (aklr/attention_bf16.h for bf16), the indexer up to its scores
// (aklr/indexer_bf16.h for bf16), index_topk (glm5/indexer.h), mla_core (glm5/mla.h) and
// row_linear_ar (aklr/row_linear_bf16.h) in one persistent kernel, as its indexer layers' kernel
// (glm5/layer.hip): one block per CU, all 256 resident at once, each waiting for the packets of the
// blocks whose outputs it reads, and each swapping its 24 output rows with the same block of every
// other rank.
// M <= 4 runs that kernel, in glm5; 6, 8, 12 and 16 the one in glm5_m16 (aklr_m16/ix_indexer_layer.h), the tokens the
// columns of the same MFMA tiles and every weight read once for all of them, the scores read once per request, on
// its own state and peer memory, after glm5's.
// source: Infera-Flash csrc/glm5 at 3b1dc45
#include <ATen/ATen.h>
#include <ATen/hip/HIPContext.h>
#include <ATen/hip/impl/HIPGuardImplMasqueradingAsCUDA.h>
#include <c10/hip/HIPException.h>
